# The source-build variant: everything the store build is, minus Konode's own Google OAuth
# client secret. Loaded by `vite build --mode source`, and Vite gives `.env.<mode>` priority
# over `.env`, so this blanks the secret without anyone having to move `.env` out of the way
# first. That move is what went wrong on 2026-08-17: the two variants were built minutes
# apart to the same path, and for a while the file labelled "ready for the store" was the one
# with no secret in it, which breaks Google Drive sign-in for every user who installs it.
#
# This file belongs in git. It holds no secret, and CI needs it: the zips attached to a
# release are source builds, and CI has no .env at all.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
